**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-dev
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.env
*.md
# Real secret-ish local-scratch directories (gitignored, never meant to
# leave the developer's own machine) that apps/api/Dockerfile's own
# `COPY apps/api apps/api` step would otherwise pick up wholesale, into
# the build stage's filesystem layers, if they happen to exist on disk at
# build time - mint-customer-token.ts (dev-scripts/) writes real Ed25519
# PRIVATE keys to .customer-keys/; the embedding smoke-test/quality-check
# scripts cache embedding vectors (not secret, but still never meant to
# ship) in .embedding-cache/. A confirmed-real gap, found by checking: at
# the time this was added, apps/api/.customer-keys/ had two real private
# key files on disk from an actual manual-testing session.
**/.customer-keys
**/.embedding-cache
# Dev-only diagnostic scripts (apps/api/dev-scripts/) never need to be in
# the Docker build context for the API image - they're excluded from
# tsconfig.build.json already, this just keeps the build context itself
# smaller. See docs/learning-notes.md for why these moved out of
# src/scripts/ in the first place.
**/dev-scripts
# This applies to the API image's build ONLY - mock-store's own real
# source IS needed by mock-store/Dockerfile (the demo profile's own
# image), which uses mock-store/Dockerfile.dockerignore instead of this
# file for that one build (a BuildKit-specific ignore file next to the
# Dockerfile REPLACES, never merges with, this root one - see that file's
# own comment). Here, for the API image, only mock-store/package.json is
# ever needed (pnpm workspace resolution), never its actual source.
mock-store/*
!mock-store/package.json
